			"claims": [
				{
					"id": "correction:fc1a3192bd69809f75492a6aa8e6432069fd201c5e47773351c2b23c8caa855d",
					"reason": "The corrected Laurent powers restore the z/3 term. The partial-fraction representation supports positivity, monotonicity and compact-interval convergence; the removable value of r(z)/z is 1/3. The Cz bound is restricted to 0<z<=pi/8, with the stated extension at zero. Inspected exact arithmetic and replay establish Cz<0.337 without relying on the superseded floating-point enclosure.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:ef698c4e149f87f152b54eb4cb1a3b2e1e5e755923c13ed7b6bf8af59b7d5b55",
					"reason": "Pole-free matching and oscillation identify the first even and odd modes before division. For R>=1500 and w>=2, z2<pi/4 forces pi/2<theta2<pi, making the delta equations legitimate. The monotonicity arguments prove the brackets, including w=2. The upper arctangent tends to pi/2 as u approaches 1/2; no global odd-phase branch or divergent arctangent is retained.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:69425b718adc1704b8e77b7211f147ee70dde70be24acadb9e633131c7735a52",
					"reason": "Under the stated R, u and w restrictions, alpha is positive, the phase comparison gives theta<t, and all denominators remain positive. The continuous estimates give d1>4alpha and d2<(2800/999)alpha<3alpha, hence G-Dbar>ell/(R*u^3). The trigonometric bound covers the entire required interval. This proof includes w=2 and does not depend on the invalid historical interval scans.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:1abf08d53cb548f101d4750539f5c2c1ee2b57edddcb23399d8e54b4d28150ba",
					"reason": "The continuous phase-speed argument supplies the claimed global gap bound and excludes the entire w<=2 region for R>=1500. Together with A'', T2 uniqueness and both endpoint limits, it proves convergence of the infimum and of near minimizers satisfying R*eta->0. The implicit-function calculation gives the fixed-interior-u 1/R term. Exact replay confirms the displayed T3 enclosures and correct endpoint-image directions. Scope remains the symmetric well family.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:c704f0b5443243081c96a35469d3649aadace73278c4f2427ecbd550bb77cbf9",
					"reason": "The recurrence decomposition proves a product lower bound rather than equality. The actual-solution diagonal criterion and explicitly restricted B=0 models have the stated critical endpoints. Both perturbed coefficients are retained, and the P2 counterexample demonstrates why bounded or eventually small perturbations are insufficient. The sufficient condition requires both parities and every index; formal differential images are distinguished from genuine operator-domain elements.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:458a02186e9a8e23d76fc42be0faa4d9943d5e073d578c5c72a31781c20a6d4c",
					"reason": "The stability proof uses its own recurrence, moment and perturbation arguments. The quotient paper's repaired c->0 representative limits are not premises of those arguments. Current source and dependency hashes match the supplied snapshots, and the renewed card preserves its conditional stability scope.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:ff0ab3ad28d7a31f6dded0143b838518577b9efa30c664c2882acdf985e88ac7",
					"reason": "The new fractional-window pointer is supported by the independently checked four-trace graph-core proof. The card explicitly separates that result from its abstract assumptions requiring all monomials in the moment space. It does not transfer perturbation completeness automatically to Krein power domains or weaken the finite-prefix conditions.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:dfe69aac1cc39c7aba7abc9859d24499f6a52e756a4ad0ec32d81a0dfdaea3e7",
					"reason": "The card now states the genuine first-derivative Krein boundary condition and distinguishes the sparse completeness family from the Gram-Schmidt orthogonal family. Its H2/H3 completeness statements are supported by the supplied operator, moment and graph-core arguments. Algebraic inversion is not identified with the boundary-constrained operator inverse, and the all-order named-polynomial interpretation remains withdrawn.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:8a7029b0cb118701bbba702e962f82d2cb96cce31de7ef87f95ccab72b400bb2",
					"reason": "The zero-parameter form has radical span{1,x}, and the Legendre derivative identity gives the diagonal Gram entries 2(2n-1). The repaired low-mode representatives tend to P2/sqrt(6) and P3/sqrt(10), with their affine discrepancies disappearing only in the quotient. Parity induction bounds the high-mode recurrence remainder by O_n(a_n), supporting divergence and fixed-index normalized limits without a uniform-in-n assertion.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:4642df3b2057e258d4056d26a993ce0165e3576b022d0af60deec33e7ab4c6f3",
					"reason": "The propagated 0<=s<7/2 window refers to the specified sparse p_n family. Nonzero leading spectral coefficients prove failure of each non-affine named member at s=7/2 and above. The card correctly allows boundary cancellation in finite combinations while retaining the withdrawal of unrestricted all-order polynomial transport.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:15a28e560194b0de108ae4fb20096ea1a92e9dbc1a593d99cc3132592efa3bd1",
					"reason": "The complete spectrum includes both affine modes and the correct sine normalization. Integration by parts yields the stated nonzero k^-4 leading coefficients for both parities, giving the sharp 7/2 threshold, including endpoint divergence. The four-trace matrix has determinant 15360; its bounded polynomial right inverse yields a graph core in D(Kc^2). Spectral truncation then proves density throughout 0<=s<7/2.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:6bd2127271b8002ba3f637e9fcfa27573d02f993a06ab4405ca1fce982db8440",
					"reason": "Direct moment transport is restricted to s=2,3, where the target moment spaces are L2 and H1 and the monomials are admissible. Both parity recurrences have B>=0 and A-B>=4m+c, giving factorial lower growth incompatible with their moment bounds. The card does not infer arbitrary-order operator action from formal polynomial differentiation.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:d5c986e8260e6d53b4e310fb6eff66de8692cdc2079abf36784819368f6ae527",
					"reason": "The formerly unresolved 3<s<7/2 window is now supported by the separate graph-core and spectral-truncation proof. The repaired dependency identifies the supplied spectral-domain version exactly. The moment method itself remains restricted to its well-defined low-order spaces, and the obstruction at s>=7/2 remains explicit.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:6d468ed87a736afdfb81282b1d434d5c0b16a920a59116ca2c4738896d7184f7",
					"reason": "The scale construction retains the positive spectral lower bound and uses genuine power domains. Negative orders are explicitly completed rather than treating an incomplete weaker norm on the original Hilbert space as complete. The isometries have the correct spectral exponents, and the Krein dependency includes the missing affine mode and proper normalization.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:76ae1aa768a6db16a98db28fb5b738ff2d8556317bb1bd50086601d9ca04b2ed",
					"reason": "The exact spectral-domain dependency matches the frozen repaired card. Its fixed-c sharp window follows from the supplied proof and is presented as a result for the specified Krein family. It does not enlarge the assumptions of the general self-adjoint scale theorem or imply uniformity as c approaches zero.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:aa949b7a06836d9ea2713484de2548807e0043e6c6600c5c6c4ce3ced54af7d8",
					"reason": "The repaired criterion explicitly requires admissible family members, pinned low moments, one remaining free moment per parity, and the stronger all-index coefficient gap. Monotonicity gives u_j/u_(j-1)>=(A_j-B_j)/c0 and the factorial bound; it does not give the false A_j/c0 bound. The isometric transport and polynomial density therefore support the stated completeness conclusion.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:c7080ba7c2ef1b2033b7dcb62e969e37acc23221d74722681cced2d7e1e80794",
					"reason": "The new range statement is attributed to the independently valid four-trace graph-core proof. It does not extend the moment-jump mechanism to undefined higher-order monomial pairings. The current dependency hashes match, and the strict upper threshold and distinction between named members and compatible combinations are preserved.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:26407866b3eb4034b240ff741a3d270995ad4a1c49b5ebbeb70a2bf89c85151a",
					"reason": "The abstract criteria retain the hypothesis that all polynomials belong to and are dense in the moment space. Both parity branches and sufficient growth conditions are required. The left-definite application uses L2/H1 moment spaces and spectral transfer, while p4 supplies the genuine higher-domain obstruction. The diagonal endpoint beta=3/2 follows from divergence of the corresponding positive series.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:22f146c8cda5ae02aad6c635fc0226ec7b8e14c846f6ef9be736be149d692380",
					"reason": "The propagated sharp window is supported by all-member spectral estimates and the four-trace core. The algebraic span is correctly Pi intersect D(Kc), not all Pi. The added qualifications prevent inferring sparse-family projection density from polynomial density alone or requiring finite moments to be injective on an entire infinite-dimensional space.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:4660445eefe6a76a2b70658964d090a0e893c9026ec4f396c040753b038c9124",
					"reason": "The structural card fixes c>0 and s=2, uses the actual Krein domain with norm ||Kc f||_2, and forms moments in L2. Its isometry and continuous central traces are justified by the supplied operator estimates. No arbitrary-order polynomial transport or tail rigidity without the missing low-mode conditions is retained.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
				},
				{
					"id": "correction:cee93c289836f3d9d4fb197a917cfe93c205619d43e7a2b9d1a5d7bdb500126b",
					"reason": "The Green functions have the required interface jumps and endpoint data, proving the value and derivative trace representations. Local zero-trace cutoff, polynomial approximation and the endpoint matrix with determinant 2L^2 establish the full-tail closure. This proves the cofinite classification and its two possible trace obstructions, including complex coefficients and non-coordinate constraints. Finite monomial deletion remains valid, with the odd substitution factor corrected to one.",
					"verdict": "APPROVED"
